  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 802.48 River corridor",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 802.48 “River corridor” means “river corridor” as defined in RSA 483:4, XVIII, namely “the river and the land area located within a distance of 1,320 feet of the normal high water mark or to the landward extent of the 100 year floodplain as designated by the Federal Emergency Management Agency, whichever distance is larger.”\n\nSource. #10998, eff 1-1-16; ss by #14571, eff 5-15-26, EXPIRES: 5-15-36 (formerly Env-Wq 802.40)",
